Being a step further from cursed is already covered.  This is not a big
deal in the early game, but by the time I reach the drawbridge of the
castle I want all of my weapons and armor blessed because from there on
it is likely to face spellcasting monsters that can hit.  If one of their
spells hits a blessed piece of armor, it becomes uncursed.  If uncursed
it becomes cursed.  If cursed the item vanishes.  Very bad.  By the time
I an deep in Genhome, I want all of the items in my regular inventory
and most of the items in my bags blessed for the same reason.

Armour eroding less is already covered.  Blessed and greased is far
better than just greased.

Blessed weapons also do more damage to monsters you start encountering
deep in the dungeon.  Again this is not an issue early on.  But facing
a vampire lord for the first time, the 2 extra hit points just might
be enough to make the difference.  Again, until you get to the drawbridge,
it doesn't apply to much.

